The depth limit applies to directory arguments only: the glob pattern `input/**/*.md` still lists every file it matches, at any depth, while the directory argument `other` is cut after one level.
== args
--depth
1
input/**/*.md
other
== file input/a/b/deep.md
# Deep
== file other/top.md
# Top
== file other/sub/below.md
# Below
== stdout
glob view: input/**/*.md other
input/a/b/deep.md (1 line): # Deep
other/sub/ (1 file, 1 line)
other/top.md (1 line): # Top
== stderr
== exit 0
